quran[8]{c,v,t}:
  3,133,"And hasten towards forgiveness from your Lord, and Paradise, whose breadth is as (vast as) the heavens and the earth, prepared for the God-conscious,"
  3,134,"those who spend in charity during times of prosperity and adversity, control their anger and excuse (the faults of) people. And Allah loves the benevolent."
  3,135,"And those who, when they commit an indecent act or wrong themselves, remember Allah and seek forgiveness for their sins. And who forgives sins besides Allah? And they do not knowingly persist in what they have done."
  3,136,Their reward is forgiveness from their Lord and Gardens with rivers flowing beneath them. They will reside in them forever. How excellent is the reward of those who perform (righteous deeds)!
  3,137,"Certain precedents (from the perished nations) have passed before you. So, travel the earth and observe the fate of the deniers."
  3,138,This (Qur’an) is an exposition for humankind—a guidance and admonition for the God-conscious.
  3,139,Do not deem yourselves weak and do not grieve (over your losses); you shall have the upper hand if you are (true) believers.
  3,140,"If injuries have afflicted you (at the Battle of Uhud, then recall that) similar injuries had already afflicted those people (at the Battle of Badr). These are the days (of victory and defeat) that We alternate between people (in turns) so that God may reveal the true believers and choose martyrs from among you. And Allah does not like the wrongdoers."
